    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "The difference in the oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math> between the oxidised product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math> formed on complete hydrolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Hydrolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> will give&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>. This hydrolysis reaction is a redox reaction. This redox reaction is an example of disproportionation reaction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><mn>4</mn><mi>Xe</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>HF</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>The oxidation states of Xenon in the reactant and product is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the difference in oxidation state is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
